{
  "manufacturer": "Teracom",
  "manufacturer_slug": "teracom",
  "model": "TDI340 4-channel S0 pulse counter with Modbus RTU",
  "model_slug": "tdi340",
  "short_model": "TDI340",
  "aliases": [
    "TDI340"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter (S0 pulse counter / digital input module)",
  "applies_to": "TDI340 per the Teracom TDI340 user manual Revision R1.11, firmware V1.06 or later.",
  "summary": "The TDI340 is a Teracom DIN-rail module with four isolated S0 inputs (IEC 62053-31) and a Modbus RTU RS-485 port. Each input has a 32-bit pulse counter in polling or edge mode, a scaled real value and an open/closed state, with optional debounce delays.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The register table prints both a PDU (wire) address and a logical address (PDU + 40001 for holding registers). 'documented' holds the logical number; the PDU number is what goes in the request, e.g. logical 40101 = PDU 100."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "V1.06 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "TDI340 User manual",
    "doc_number": "Revision R1.11",
    "revision_date": "2026-10",
    "url": "https://www.teracomsystems.com/download/s0-pulse-counter-with-modbus-rtu-interface-tdi340-user-manual/",
    "pages": "pp. 5-7 (Modbus address table)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are taken from the manual's PDU address column (0-based); the logical column adds 40001 for holding registers and 10001 for discrete inputs, as the manual states.",
    "All 32-bit values follow the Data order register (PDU 13): 1 = most significant word first (factory default), 2 = least significant word first. The map shows the default, ABCD.",
    "Left out: the 32-bit float/integer test-value registers (PDU 82-95), which only exist to check word order; the 16-bit test values are kept.",
    "Input states are also readable as discrete inputs PDU 1-4 (logical 10002-10005), as the table prints them.",
    "Debounce delays (0-65535 x 10 ms) only work while that input's counter is in polling mode.",
    "A missing float returns NaN and a missing 32-bit integer -2147483648."
  ],
